From: Wolf Vollprecht <w.vollprecht@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] isaac_ros_common: do not inject CCCL into every link interface

CCCL is header-only, but link_libraries(CCCL::CCCL) applies directory-wide and
therefore injects the target into every subsequently created target. In
particular, rosidl-generated targets export CCCL::CCCL from their installed
CMake files without also exporting a find_dependency(CCCL) call. Downstream
find_package then fails because the imported target does not exist.

Add CCCL's toolkit include directory directly instead. This provides the same
headers without contaminating unrelated installed link interfaces.
---
 isaac_ros_common/cmake/isaac_ros_common-extras.cmake | 8 +-------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/isaac_ros_common/cmake/isaac_ros_common-extras.cmake b/isaac_ros_common/cmake/isaac_ros_common-extras.cmake
--- a/isaac_ros_common/cmake/isaac_ros_common-extras.cmake
+++ b/isaac_ros_common/cmake/isaac_ros_common-extras.cmake
@@ -36,13 +36,7 @@ find_package(CUDAToolkit REQUIRED)
 include_directories("${CUDAToolkit_INCLUDE_DIRS}")

 # CUDA 13 CCCL migration: ensure host compiler can find <cuda/std/...>, <thrust/...>, <cub/...>
-# Prefer linking the CCCL CMake target when available; otherwise add CTK's cccl include path.
-find_package(CCCL CONFIG QUIET)
-if(TARGET CCCL::CCCL)
-  link_libraries(CCCL::CCCL)
-else()
-  include_directories("${CUDAToolkit_INCLUDE_DIRS}/cccl")
-endif()
+include_directories("${CUDAToolkit_INCLUDE_DIRS}/cccl")

 # Setup cuda architectures
 # Target Ada is CUDA 11.8 or greater
